  <static seed="1932" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers60.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p>Do not use a calculator.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{144} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{1.44} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{0.0144} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>12</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.12</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>First, recognize that <m>144</m> is a square number. Since <m>12\cdot12=144</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{144}=12</m>.</p>
<p>Next, since <m>1.2\cdot1.2=1.44</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{1.44}=1.2</m>.</p>
<p>Finally, since <m>0.12\cdot0.12=0.0144</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{0.0144}=0.12</m>.</p>
</solution>
